<LegalLayout title="Centrix Data Protection Statement" description="Centrix controller and processor responsibilities, safeguards and data handling.">
  <p>Centrix handles personal data as part of its own business activities and when providing IT services to clients. This statement explains the responsibilities and safeguards that guide that work. Centrix is based at Downestown, Duleek, Co. Meath, Ireland.</p>
  <p>Contact our Data Protection Officer at <a href="mailto:data@centrix.ie">data@centrix.ie</a>. Report suspected exposures or security incidents to <a href="mailto:security@centrix.ie">security@centrix.ie</a>.</p>
  <h2>1 Controller and processor responsibilities</h2>
  <p>Centrix is a controller for its own enquiries, marketing, business administration and other purposes explained in the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Notice</a>. A client normally remains the controller for personal data in systems it asks Centrix to administer. Where we handle that information only on the client’s documented instructions, we act as processor.</p>
  <p>Roles depend on the actual activity. Any separate or joint controller responsibility must be identified and addressed for that engagement. The client determines its lawful purposes, notices and retention requirements and must have authority to grant access.</p>
  <h2>2 Processing agreements and instructions</h2>
  <p>Before processing client personal data as a processor, the parties must have a binding agreement meeting Article 28 GDPR. It must address the processing scope, duration, purposes, data types, affected people, instructions, confidentiality, security, subprocessors, assistance, breaches, audit information and return or deletion.</p>
  <p>This public statement does not replace that agreement or authorise system access. Centrix processes client data only within authorised instructions, except where applicable law requires otherwise. We must alert the client if, in our opinion, an instruction infringes applicable data protection law.</p>
  <h2>3 Data minimisation and security</h2>
  <p>Access and copies must be limited to what the task requires. Our requirements for each engagement cover appropriate access permissions, authentication, confidentiality, secure communication and credential handling, logging, system protection, recovery and access removal. The agreed scope identifies which controls are operated by Centrix, the client or a provider.</p>
  <p>Sensitive records, including health information, children’s data and criminal offence data, need specific assessment and suitable safeguards. Detailed security arrangements belong in the service’s security schedule. This statement is not a claim of certification or an assurance that incidents cannot occur.</p>
  <h2>4 AI use</h2>
  <p>Centrix does not submit customer information to AI tools. Client AI consultancy or deployment work requires its own agreed scope and assessment of data flows, access, retention and provider terms before personal data is used. A provider logo on our website is not permission to disclose client data to that provider.</p>
  <h2>5 Providers and international processing</h2>
  <p>Our website and communications arrangements use Cloudflare, GitHub and Microsoft as described in the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Notice</a>. Suppliers used for a particular client service are assessed separately. A client’s direct provider is not automatically a Centrix subprocessor.</p>
  <p>A subprocessor requires the client’s prior specific or general written authorisation and appropriate contractual obligations. General authorisation must provide notice of intended additions or replacements and an opportunity to object. Clients can request the relevant supplier list and processing locations at <a href="mailto:data@centrix.ie">data@centrix.ie</a>.</p>
  <p>International storage, support access and onward transfers must have a lawful basis and any required safeguards. Provider networks can involve processing outside the EEA, including the United States. Any specific location restriction must be agreed and verified for the service concerned.</p>
  <h2>6 Incidents and breaches</h2>
  <p>When acting as processor, Centrix must notify the client without undue delay after becoming aware of a personal data breach, provide available information and support the response. Notification must not wait until an investigation is complete. The client agreement identifies escalation contacts and any additional deadlines.</p>
  <p>Where Centrix is controller, a breach must be notified to the competent supervisory authority without undue delay and, where feasible, within 72 hours of awareness unless it is unlikely to pose a risk to people’s rights and freedoms. Affected people must be informed without undue delay where a high risk is likely, subject to lawful exceptions.</p>
  <h2>7 Rights and compliance assistance</h2>
  <p>Requests concerning Centrix-controlled data go to <a href="mailto:data@centrix.ie">data@centrix.ie</a>. Requests about client-controlled data should normally go to the client. We support the client under the processing agreement, including appropriate assistance with rights requests, security, breach notifications, impact assessments and regulator consultation.</p>
  <h2>8 Retention and service exit</h2>
  <p>Our own business records follow the periods in the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Notice</a>. Routine support tickets are retained for 24 months after closure; temporary client data copied for support is deleted within 30 days of completing the task or sooner if the client agreement requires. Deleted data in Centrix-controlled backups expires within 90 days.</p>
  <p>At service exit, client personal data is returned or deleted at the client’s choice under the agreement unless law requires retention. Any backup cycle or legal exception must be addressed in that agreement. Access removal and handover form part of exit planning. Key contract records do not justify retaining full client datasets.</p>
  <p>For concerns, contact <a href="mailto:data@centrix.ie">data@centrix.ie</a>. You may also contact the Irish Data Protection Commission at <a href="https://www.dataprotection.ie/">https://www.dataprotection.ie/</a>. We update this statement when our arrangements change.</p>
</LegalLayout>
